mia-docs: Drafting relnotes for the 'strict_json' output mode — we now validate structured responses against the declared output schema and return an explicit `schema_mismatch` warning instead of silent best-effort coercion. Putting migration tips and SDK snippet updates here for review before I open the PR.

zack-eng: important: runtime will start returning 422 for hard schema failures in v2.0.0; add compatibility note and a fallback pattern customers can use.

ola-sdk: SDK change: js >=2.3 will include `strictJson: true/false` in the client options; python uses `strict_json=True/False`. We should show old vs new and a recommended soft-fail pattern that logs mismatches and falls back to `raw_text`.

mia-docs: adding snippets. Old (loose behavior):
```js
// old: best-effort conversion, no explicit warnings
const resp = await client.chat.completions.create({
  model: 'kestrel-4',
  messages,
  output_schema: { type: 'object', properties: { name: { type: 'string' } } }
});
```

New (recommended):
```js
// new: opt-in strict validation and soft-fail pattern
try {
  const resp = await client.chat.completions.create({
    model: 'kestrel-4',
    messages,
    output_schema: schema,
    options: { strictJson: true }
  });
  if (resp.warning === 'schema_mismatch') {
    // fallback: log and use raw_text
    console.warn('Schema mismatch, falling back to raw_text');
    use(resp.raw_text);
  } else {
    use(resp.parsed);
  }
} catch (err) {
  if (err.code === 422) {
    // hard failure: decide fallback
    useLastKnownGood();
  }
}
```

mia-docs: Python snippet: 
```py
# new: strict_json option and soft-fail
try:
    resp = client.chat.completions.create(
        model='kestrel-4',
        messages=messages,
        output_schema=schema,
        options={'strict_json': True}
    )
    if resp.get('warning') == 'schema_mismatch':
        # fallback to raw_text
        logger.warning('schema mismatch, using raw_text')
        handle(resp['raw_text'])
    else:
        handle(resp['parsed'])
except ApiError as e:
    if e.status_code == 422:
        handle_last_good()
```

rachel-prod: Product note: this is a breaking-but-valuable change for structured tooling integrations. Recommend we add a clear what's-new blurb and a migration checklist: 1) pin SDK to compatible versions 2) add `strict_json` opt-in and a fallback path 3) run schema regression tests. Also include guidance for model authors to tighten schemas gradually.

harry-support: Support found two customers impacted in alpha who had post-processing that assumed coercion. Ticket #8277 and #8282. Suggest putting a short Support template into the PR so agents can copy/paste steps to triage.

ola-sdk: also include a tiny helper snippet in the docs repo: `safe_parse_schema(resp)` that tries parsed, validates, and returns a tuple (ok, value, warning). Will add to examples/compat.

zack-eng: runtime footnote: the `schema_mismatch` warning includes a diff payload that may contain PII in rare cases; add security note to scrub diffs or encourage orgs to enable redact_diffs in team settings. Pin runtime >= v2.0.0 for full headers.

mia-docs: noting that. Also we discovered a broken internal link in the structured output guide after the site refactor — anchor changed from `#json-guides` to `#structured-output`. I'll add a redirect entry in the PR. Support ticket #8210 reported it.

rachel-prod: Marketing will prepare a short banner and a checklist for enterprise customers; schedule the relnote publish for Mon 09:00 PT and add an explicit deprecation window for the old permissive behavior (30 days).

sitebot: mia-docs pushed branch mia/strict-json-relnotes -> staging/docs (CI: linkcheck failed: broken anchor redirect) :x:

mia-docs: ack. fixing redirect and adding Support template + `safe_parse_schema` example in the PR. Draft PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/7499 — includes snippets, migration checklist, security note, support template, and redirect.

ola-sdk: one more SDK nuance: server-side middleware will expose `x-schema-status` header for observability; show how to surface that in examples (JS fetch + Python requests).

mia-docs: adding header examples and a small observability snippet for the Console docs (how to filter schema warnings in the audit log).

harry-support: once merged, we should proactively message customers with open streaming/tooling integrations >500 calls/day. I'll compile the list and send to Support Ops.

mia-docs: thanks all. I'll re-run CI after redirects and aim to merge when green. Planning to publish relnotes Mon 09:00 PT. Will post the live URL and publish timestamp here when done. Closing thread for now.
